    "title": "The artifact architecture of Golmet",
    "html": "<p align=\"center\">English | <a href=\"artefatos.pt-br.md\">Português (Brasil)</a></p><h1>The artifact architecture of Golmet</h1>\n<p>The whole structure of Golmet — the directories, the formats, the\nvalidations — exists to sustain a chain of documents where <strong>each one is\nborn from another and feeds the next ones</strong>. This page tells that chain as\na story (the same journey as the\n<a href=\"/docs/getting-started/00-por-que-golmet\">tutorials</a>, seen from above) and\ncloses with the complete reference table.</p>\n<h2>The story: the seed and the descent</h2>\n<p><strong>The charter is the seed.</strong> The <code>PROJECT_CHARTER.md</code> declares what the\nproduct is — and where its code comes from (the Repos table of §1).\nEverything in the MeuApp workspace descends from the charter: it is the\nfirst document, and that is why <code>golmet validate</code> complains when it is\nmissing or unreadable — no seed, no tree.</p>\n<p><strong>REQUIREMENTS inherits and expands.</strong> The product&#39;s business rules (the\n<code>## RN-NNN</code> sections) are a refinement of the charter: the charter says\n&quot;it&#39;s a scheduling product&quot;, the RNs say &quot;booking with slot confirmation,\n15-minute window&quot;. Confirmed RNs are the <strong>only</strong> foundation of\nimplementation — a Feature can only be born anchored to an RN\n(<code>anchor: RN-001</code>); anchoring to a PEND is a blocking error (H1). It is the\nrule that keeps the team from implementing what nobody confirmed.</p>\n<p><strong>Specs derive from the RNs.</strong> Each RN with implementation ahead earns the\nfolder <code>analysis/RN-NNN — title/</code> with the functional and technical\nanalysis — the HOW. The spec is written from the rule (never the other way\naround): when a spec diverges from its RN, either the spec is <code>stale</code> (and\nmust declare by which CR), or there was a derivation mistake. That is why\nthe FORMAT has section §7.7: the <code>specs/DATA_MODEL.md</code> aggregate grows with\nmaturity, and the break by micro-context exists so whoever implements one\nRN doesn&#39;t have to load the whole bank.</p>\n<p><strong>The delivery delivers.</strong> The Feature in\n<code>delivery/&lt;group&gt;/RN-NNN — title — Feature.md</code> is the moving part: tasks\nwith state and owner, execution coordinated by the dev skills. The feature\nmoving is what raises the RN to <code>active</code> — with evidence\n(<code>[path:line @hash]</code>), the file+line+commit bond with the code.</p>\n<p><strong>The evidence is the seal.</strong> And here is Golmet&#39;s difference from any\ntraditional doc: RN-001 doesn&#39;t say &quot;was implemented&quot; — it <strong>points</strong> at\nthe code, and <code>golmet validate</code> confirms the pointing is real (the file\nexists, the line exists, the hash is the HEAD — H7, S2). Documentation the\nmachine verifies is the only kind the team keeps trusting.</p>\n<p><strong>The index is the memory of states.</strong> The <code>golmet.index.json</code> keeps every\nentity&#39;s state at the last good validation. When a confirmed rule changes,\nthe path is the CR (<code>CHANGE_REQUESTS.md</code> records the change, the RN\nupdates, the spec drops to <code>stale</code> with the reason); when a technical\ndecision is made, it becomes an ADR in <code>DECISIONS.md</code> — immutable, because\nthe history of &quot;why&quot; is what the team will re-read.</p>\n<p><strong>And what closes the knowledge circle</strong>: the TRACEABILITY (in <code>quality/</code>)\nmaps RN → generated documents; the knowledge pack (patterns, domains,\nrules) inherits what the project revealed — the chain doesn&#39;t end at the\ndelivery, it ends by becoming an organizational asset.</p>\n<h2>The reference table</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Document</th>\n<th>Where it lives</th>\n<th>Feeds</th>\n<th>Is fed by</th>\n<th>Produced by (<code>gm-*</code>)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>PROJECT_CHARTER.md</code></td>\n<td>workspace root</td>\n<td>REQUIREMENTS, specs, everything</td>\n<td>the founding conversation</td>\n<td><code>gm-charter</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>REQUIREMENTS.md</code> (RNs + PENDs)</td>\n<td>root</td>\n<td>specs, delivery (the anchors)</td>\n<td>charter + elicitation with the owner</td>\n<td><code>gm-req</code> (via <code>gm-clarify</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>CHANGE_REQUESTS.md</code> (CRs)</td>\n<td>root</td>\n<td>RNs (the update), specs (the staleness)</td>\n<td>post-confirmation changes</td>\n<td><code>gm-req</code> (<code>gm-change-request</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>DECISIONS.md</code> (ADRs)</td>\n<td>root</td>\n<td>the technical decisions of specs</td>\n<td>the architecture discussion</td>\n<td><code>gm-decision-log</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>analysis/RN-NNN/</code> (functional + technical)</td>\n<td>analysis/</td>\n<td>the Feature and the tasks</td>\n<td>the RNs</td>\n<td><code>gm-taskspec</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>specs/DATA_MODEL.md</code> etc.</td>\n<td>specs/</td>\n<td>implementation, db drift</td>\n<td>the RNs</td>\n<td><code>gm-datamodel</code>, <code>gm-apicontracts</code>, <code>gm-arch</code>, <code>gm-uispec</code>, <code>gm-criteria</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>delivery/RN-NNN — Feature.md</code></td>\n<td>delivery/</td>\n<td>the code (the tasks)</td>\n<td>the technical analysis</td>\n<td><code>gm-taskspec</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>golmet.index.json</code></td>\n<td>root</td>\n<td>the validate comparisons</td>\n<td>the prose (the kit writes)</td>\n<td>the kit (<code>golmet validate</code>/<code>index</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>quality/TRACEABILITY.md</code></td>\n<td>quality/</td>\n<td>the coverage audit</td>\n<td>everything</td>\n<td><code>gm-traceability</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>knowledge pack (<code>rules/</code>, <code>accumulation/</code>, <code>domains/</code>)</td>\n<td>the org&#39;s pack</td>\n<td>the next projects</td>\n<td>retrospectives and decisions</td>\n<td><code>gm-rule-keeper</code>, <code>gm-pattern-extractor</code>, <code>gm-domain-research</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>The rules that sustain the chain</h2>\n<p>The chain is only worth it if it&#39;s verified. The <a href=\"../../docs/FORMAT.md\">FORMAT v1</a>\ndefines the checks that keep it from rotting: H1 (PEND never anchors a\nFeature), H3 (a ready Feature requires an active RN), H4 (an active RN\nrequires evidence), H7 (the evidence resolves in the code), H10\n(cross-references resolve), H8 (the state in the index is the history — an\naccepted ADR doesn&#39;t change). The soft (S1–S5) and the lint (L1–L10) watch\nthe rest — the full discipline in <a href=\"../../docs/FORMAT.md\">FORMAT §9</a>.</p>\n",
