    "title": "The init wizard — what happens on screen",
    "html": "<p align=\"center\">English | <a href=\"init.pt-br.md\">Português (Brasil)</a></p><h1>The init wizard — what happens on screen</h1>\n<p>Tutorial <a href=\"/docs/getting-started/01-organizacao\">01</a> showed the wizard in\naction. This page documents the mechanism — the guarantees the wizard gives\nand the ones you can demand from it.</p>\n<h2>The principle: never creates without asking</h2>\n<p><strong>Bare <code>golmet init</code> is always interactive</strong> — it asks, shows the summary,\nand only creates on ENTER at the confirm. It is the kit&#39;s answer to the\naccident that motivated the rule: an init run in the wrong folder (the\nHOME, next to the kit&#39;s global installation) created a workspace mixed with\nthe kit&#39;s own state. Hence: <strong>the init never creates at the HOME root</strong>,\nand scripts/CI require explicit flags (<code>--org</code> or <code>--into &lt;container&gt;</code>)\nwith <code>--yes</code> — without a TTY and without flags, the init fails closed\n(exit 2, nothing written, the remediation cites the flags).</p>\n<h2>The guarantees at any step</h2>\n<p>The whole wizard runs in raw mode (the same arsenal as install), and the\nguarantees are transversal: <strong>esc/CTRL+C cancel everything, at any step</strong> —\nnothing is created before the final confirm. <strong>← on empty text goes back to\nthe previous step</strong>, with the typed value <strong>pre-echoed for editing</strong>; <code>n</code> at\nthe confirm also goes back to editing (it does not cancel). Text fields\naccept UTF-8 (accents) and backspace erases the whole character — in raw\nmode the keyboard ESC reaches the program, something the console captures\nin cooked mode.</p>\n<h2>The recommended mode in practice</h2>\n<p>For those who prefer the fast path, the flags are the wizard as a command:\n<code>golmet init --org</code> (declares the org, creates the <code>.gitignore</code>, registers\nin the global catalog) and <code>golmet init &lt;produto&gt; --into &lt;container&gt;</code>\n(delivers the product in the org&#39;s declared versioning model). <code>--yes</code>\nskips confirmation with explicit flags. The full declaration of the paths\nis in <a href=\"../../docs/FORMAT.md\">FORMAT §2</a> and in the reference\n(<a href=\"/docs/reference/commands\">commands.md</a>).</p>\n",
    "translated": true
