    "slug": "concepts/knowledge",
    "base": "concepts/knowledge",
    "locale": "en",
    "lang": "en",
    "group": "Concepts",
    "title": "The knowledge ecosystem",
    "html": "<p align=\"center\">English | <a href=\"knowledge.pt-br.md\">Português (Brasil)</a></p><h1>The knowledge ecosystem</h1>\n<p>Tutorial <a href=\"/docs/getting-started/05-maturity-and-knowledge\">05</a> told what\nremains when the project ends. This page opens the ecosystem: where the\nknowledge lives, who writes into it, and how an artifact finds its place.</p>\n<h2>The three shelves of the state pack</h2>\n<p>MinhaOrganizacao&#39; knowledge lives in a <strong>state pack</strong> — a Git repository cloned at\n<code>packs/&lt;id&gt;/</code> in the engine config, inherited by the team via\n<code>golmet pack update</code>. Inside it, three shelves with defined owners and\nformats: <strong><code>domains/</code></strong> (the foundation — domain knowledge researched from\nprimary sources, with URL and access date, written by <code>gm-domain-research</code>\nBEFORE any component consumes the domain), <strong><code>accumulation/</code></strong> (the\nlearning — patterns extracted by <code>gm-pattern-extractor</code>, metrics by\n<code>gm-metrics-collector</code>, nuances by <code>gm-nuance-collector</code>) and <strong><code>rules/</code></strong>\n(the norms with triggers, written by <code>gm-rule-keeper</code> — see\n<a href=\"/docs/concepts/profile\">profile.md</a>).</p>\n<p>The separation isn&#39;t bureaucracy — each shelf has a different life cycle:\nthe foundation changes slowly (the domain doesn&#39;t change every week), the\nlearning grows with every project, the norms consolidate when the team\ndecides.</p>\n<h2>The router: where it goes</h2>\n<p>Mid-work, an artifact appears with no obvious destination — the discovery\n&quot;we deploy this way&quot; could be a nuance, a pattern or a norm. The question\nis not the operator&#39;s: the router (the <code>gm-knowledge-route</code> skill, guided by\nthe AGENTS.md T1–T5 table) classifies the fit and <strong>delegates to the\ncanonical writer</strong> — each shelf has ONE writer, never two. The central\nrule: <strong>route, never replicate</strong> — each shelf has its own index, and\ncopying content between them is the road to knowledge rotting into two\ndifferent versions.</p>\n<p><strong>The escape valve</strong> covers what fits nothing: the artifact is born in the\nwork zone (<code>.golmet/</code>) — never loose — and is promoted when it gains a\nfunction, with the canonical writer responsible for the promotion.</p>\n<h2>Why a pack and not a loose folder</h2>\n<p>A state pack is a Git repository of its own: <code>pack publish</code> pushes to the\nremote, <code>pack update</code> pulls for the team — with auto-commit of the local\naccumulation and rebase, and the kit <strong>never discards</strong> what the team\naccumulated. That is the difference between knowledge living in a file\nnobody versions and knowledge living in a versioned organizational asset.</p>\n",
