    "group": "Concepts",
    "title": "The content layers",
    "html": "<p align=\"center\">English | <a href=\"layers.pt-br.md\">Português (Brasil)</a></p><h1>The content layers</h1>\n<p>The first question from anyone adopting the kit is &quot;where does what my AI\ncarries come from?&quot; — and the answer is a scale of four layers, weakest to\nstrongest: <strong>L0 embedded</strong> (the minimal BASE inside the binary — offline),\n<strong>L1 FULL</strong> (the 93 workflow components, embedded), <strong>L2 packs</strong> (the\norganization overlays and the knowledge state packs) and <strong>L3 local</strong> (the\noperator&#39;s creations). When two layers provide the same component, the\nprecedence is: <strong>local &gt; pack &gt; full &gt; base</strong> — your fine-tuning wins, the\nembedded loses.</p>\n<h2>The two profiles — and the operator&#39;s choice</h2>\n<p>When the operator ran <code>golmet install --engine opencode</code> (tutorial\n<a href=\"/docs/getting-started/00-por-que-golmet\">00</a>), the wizard asked for the\n<strong>profile</strong>. <code>essencial</code> installs L0+BASE into the workspace <code>.golmet/</code>\nzone — the kit becomes versioned in the repository and the team inherits by\ncloning; it works on any agentic engine. <code>completo</code> materializes L1 FULL\ninto the engine — the 93 components (agents, skills, profiles, templates)\nlive in Opencode, and it is the recommended mode because nothing is\nmissing: the AI enters the workspace with the whole workflow.</p>\n<p>Local customization of a managed file is detected and <strong>preserved</strong> — the\ncontent manifest knows every file&#39;s provenance and SHA-256; overwriting\nwhat the operator modified requires an explicit <code>--force</code>.</p>\n<h2>The <code>.golmet/</code> zone changes role</h2>\n<p>The same kit folder, different semantics by context — and that is by\ndesign: in the <strong>product workspace</strong>, <code>.golmet/</code> is the repo-versioned kit\n(DR-008); in the <strong>engine config</strong>, it&#39;s kit state (the content manifest\nand the personal.json); in an <strong>org-repo Organization</strong>, it&#39;s the gitignored\nwork zone (checkpoints in <code>meetings/</code>, history in <code>migrations/</code>) — with the\nversioned exception <code>.golmet/skills/</code> when the org essential runs at the\nroot (see <a href=\"/docs/concepts/organization\">organization.md</a>).</p>\n<p>What it means in MeuApp&#39;s practice: the product carries no zone of its own —\nthe zone is MinhaOrganizacao&#39;. If the org ever moved to <code>produtos-repo</code>, each\nproduct would gain its own (<code>init --into</code> delivers the declared model — the\ndetail in <a href=\"/docs/reference/commands\">docs/reference/commands.md</a>).</p>\n",
